              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case concerns the proper standard for the state\u2011of\u2011mind element in a claim of inducing patent infringement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8bf6088c85e002e83dc688854e97ccc6eb234dca185196d00bbf2740b7d91ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8bf6088c85e0-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that liability should require a purposeful, culpable intent to induce infringement, meaning the inducer must intend the infringing act and know the patent is infringed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8bf6088c85e002e83dc688854e97ccc6eb234dca185196d00bbf2740b7d91ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8bf6088c85e0-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners contend that willful blindness does not satisfy this purposeful, culpable test."
      }
    ],
